development.question_text:
Sand is poured onto the top of a conical pile at $4$ m³/min. The pile always makes an angle of $45^{\circ}$ with the ground, so its radius equals its height. At what rate is the height rising when the height is $2$ m?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.5);
\coordinate (L) at (-2.5,0);
\coordinate (R) at (2.5,0);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (L) -- (A);
\draw (A) -- (R);
\draw (L) arc (180:360:2.5 and 0.6);
\draw[dashed] (L) arc (180:0:2.5 and 0.6);
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (O) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (R) node[midway, below] {$r$};
\pic[draw, "$45^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.9cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = O--A--R};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A tank has the shape of a cone standing on its vertex, $12$ m deep with a top radius of $3$ m. Water is poured in at $5$ m³/min. At what rate is the depth of water rising when the water is $4$ m deep?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.3]
\coordinate (V) at (0,0);
\coordinate (L) at (-1,4);
\coordinate (R) at (1,4);
\coordinate (T) at (0,4);
\coordinate (WC) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (WR) at (0.6,2.4);
\coordinate (WL) at (-0.6,2.4);
\draw (L) -- (V);
\draw (V) -- (R);
\draw (L) arc (180:360:1 and 0.28);
\draw[dashed] (L) arc (180:0:1 and 0.28);
\draw (WL) arc (180:360:0.6 and 0.17);
\draw[dashed] (WL) arc (180:0:0.6 and 0.17);
\draw[dashed] (V) -- (WC) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw[dashed] (WC) -- (T);
\draw[dashed] (WC) -- (WR) node[midway, above] {$r$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (T) -- (R) node[midway, above] {$3$ m};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (1.7,0) -- (1.7,4) node[midway, right] {$12$ m};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A ladder $5$ m long leans against a vertical wall. Its foot slides away from the wall at $0.6$ m/s. At what rate is the top of the ladder moving when the foot is $3$ m from the wall?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,4);
\coordinate (B) at (3,0);
\draw (0,-0.1) -- (0,4.7);
\draw (-0.6,0) -- (3.8,0);
