mastery.question_text:
Gravel falling from a chute forms a cone whose base radius is always twice its height. At what rate must the gravel be delivered if the height is to rise at $0.05$ m/min at the moment the height is $3$ m? Leave your answer in terms of $\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1.6);
\coordinate (L) at (-3.2,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw (L) -- (A);
\draw (A) -- (R);
\draw (L) arc (180:360:3.2 and 0.7);
\draw[dashed] (L) arc (180:0:3.2 and 0.7);
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (O) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (R) node[midway, below] {$r = 2h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A boat is hauled towards a dock by a rope that runs over a pulley $4$ m above the water. The rope is pulled in at $0.5$ m/s. At what rate is the boat approaching the dock when it is $3$ m away?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\coordinate (Pu) at (0,4);
\coordinate (Bt) at (3,0);
\draw (-0.6,0) -- (4,0);
\draw (D) -- (Pu) node[midway, left] {$4$ m};
\draw (Pu) -- (Bt) node[midway, above right] {$L$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-0.7) -- (3,-0.7) node[midway, below] {$x$};
\coordinate (p) at ($(D)!0.35cm!(Pu)$);
\coordinate (q) at ($(D)!0.35cm!(Bt)$);
\draw (p) -- ($(p)+(q)-(D)$) -- (q);
